CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ function template: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ lvalue parameters: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ forwarding references: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ member function template: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The fold reduction in typecheck_type required exactly one pack_size_map
entry; typecheck_function_template seeds an empty-pack entry for every
declared function template, so a second template with a pack blocked it (a
regression since d568a30139).  The pack is now chosen by the current
template scope, its placeholders are lvalues, and a callee name in the
pattern is not taken for the pack.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
